diff --git a/substack/04_explore_exploit_tradeoff.md b/substack/04_explore_exploit_tradeoff.md
index b596084..986bdfe 100644
--- a/substack/04_explore_exploit_tradeoff.md
+++ b/substack/04_explore_exploit_tradeoff.md
@@ -91,6 +91,8 @@ The first term is exploitation: favour arms that have paid off well. The second
 
 This is called **optimism in the face of uncertainty**. By acting as if each arm is as good as it plausibly could be, we're forced to explore uncertain arms. Once we've pulled an arm enough times, the confidence interval shrinks, the upper bound collapses toward the true mean, and exploitation takes over naturally.
 
+![Five arms (A-E) scored by UCB across two moments in the same run: early on (t = 12), arm D has been pulled only once and its wide uncertainty bonus gives it the highest UCB score despite a middling estimate; late on (t = 150), the confidence intervals have narrowed enough that the arm with the best true average, A, wins outright and the exploration bonus has faded out.](images/fig_t3_ucb_arms.svg)
+
